Qualcomm ESS/PPE/EDMA/UNIPHY in-tree ethernet port (E phase)

Provenance: upstream OpenWrt master (openwrt/openwrt, mid-2026,
qualcommax still on kernel 6.18), target/linux:
- `generic/pending-6.18/737-01..737-07` - net core prerequisites that
  are NOT in mainline 6.18.49: phylink internal-PCS handling,
  phylink_release_pcs, firmware-node (fwnode) support for PCS
  drivers, late PCS attach, pcs-handle dt-binding, `.pcs_link_down`.
  Preceded by `generic/backport-6.18/703-01,703-02` (v7.0 phylink
  resolve/helpers refactors, also not in 6.18.49).
- `qualcommax/patches-6.18/0950..0953` - wiring: DSA out-of-band
  tagging protocol, UNIPHY PCS driver (Kconfig/Makefile), PPE switch
  driver, EDMA driver.
- `qualcommax/patches-6.18/0080/0082/0191` - IPQ6018 CMN PLL
  dt-bindings + driver data + keep-bus-clocks (base driver
  `ipq-cmn-pll.c` is already mainlined in 6.18).
- `qualcommax/patches-6.18/0904/0917` - gcc-ipq6018 networking-clock
  workarounds.
- `qualcommax/files/...` - driver/dts sources, fetched at build time
  (qca_edma, qca_ppe_main/scheduler/vlan, pcs-qca-uniphy,
  ipq6018-ess.dtsi, headers). They are NOT in this tree: `./SOURCES.nix`
  holds the pin, the per-file blob sha and sha256, and `default.nix`
  installs them into the kernel tree.

Layout & usage (all done in `kernel.extraPatchPhase` of
devices/jdcloud-ax6600/default.nix; in this wired-only branch there are
no wifi patches underneath - the radio patches that the ax6600 branch
stacks this port on top of are not present here):

    fetch each file and patch from the pin in ../SOURCES.nix
    install the files into the kernel root
    apply the patches in the order listed in ./SOURCES.nix
    apply fixups.patch            (0950's failed hunks + one Kconfig line)
    sentinel greps verify the result

`ether/src/` and `ether/patches/` no longer exist. What is left here is
what the port owns: `fixups.patch` and these two documents.

Order (matters): 703-01, 703-02, 737-01 .. 737-07, 0080, 0082, 0191,
0904, 0917, 0950, 0951, 0952, 0953. Two of them do not apply whole to
mainline 6.18.49, because their contexts assume OpenWrt's cumulative net
tree, but only one of the two needs anything from us:

- `0950`: mainline 6.18.49 has no MXL862 DSA tags, so DSA_TAG_PROTO_OOB
  is appended with value 32, and the CONFIG_NET_DSA_TAG_OOB / net/dsa.h
  includes are inserted in skbuff.c. Both are in `fixups.patch` - without
  them `net/dsa/tag_oob.c` and the SKB_EXT_DSA_OOB entry do not compile.
- `737-02`: its last hunk (the guard around the PCS handover in
  phylink_major_config) also fails, but the patch's own earlier hunks
  already applied that handover, and the guard tests `mac_select_pcs`,
  which this stack never implements. It is deliberately NOT supplied;
  see the head of `fixups.patch`.

`fixups.patch` also carries `select PAGE_POOL` for QCOM_EDMA: the pinned
0953 leaves that dependency implicit, and upstream only gets away with it
because their target config sets `CONFIG_PAGE_POOL=y`. It has to be a
Kconfig select and cannot be a line in our kernel config, because mainline
declares PAGE_POOL with no prompt and kconfig ignores .config for promptless
symbols.

kernel config enables: NET_DSA, NET_DSA_TAG_OOB, PCS_QCA_UNIPHY,
QCOM_80211AX_PPE, QCOM_EDMA, IPQ_CMN_PLL (all =y, so the DSA ports
register at boot).

Board side (done): the board dts includes ipq6018-ess.dtsi and enables
the qca8075-package PHYs / uniphy0+1 / switch ports (swport1..5:
lan1-4 psgmii via QCA8075, wan 2500base-x via QCA8081) / edma,
modelled on OpenWrt dts/ipq6010-re-cs-02.dts. See
../ipq6010-jdcloud-re-cs-02.dts (ethernet section) and ../BRINGUP.md.

Historical alternative routes (qca-ssdk/qca-nss-dp external modules;
staying on 6.12 with a full net-core backport) were rejected in
favour of this in-tree 6.18 port; see BRINGUP.md E section.
